<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Psalm 6.18.0 - configuracao "completa" (maximo de verificacoes do nucleo,
  sem plugins).

  errorLevel="1": todas as questoes com nivel > 0 viram erro
  (Config::getReportingLevelForFile: nivel da questao < nivel configurado => info).

  Opcoes de codigo nao usado, todas ligadas:
    findUnusedCode, findUnusedVariablesAndParams, findUnusedPsalmSuppress,
    findUnusedBaselineEntry, findUnusedIssueHandlerSuppression.

  limitMethodComplexity="true" (opt-in, config.xsd default="false"): liga
  ComplexMethod/ComplexFunction (StatementsAnalyzer::checkUnreferencedVars),
  com os limites padrao maxGraphSize=200 e maxAvgPathLength=70 (Config.php).
  Incluido porque e a unica opcao opt-in do nucleo que corresponde a CS do
  catalogo (C18/C19, de forma aproximada). Remova-o para uma "completa" que
  mexa so no nivel e nas opcoes de codigo nao usado.

  Nao incluidos (opt-in do nucleo sem relacao com os 38 CS):
  checkForThrowsDocblock, checkForThrowsInGlobalScope,
  ensureArrayIntOffsetsExist, ensureArrayStringOffsetsExist,
  disallowLiteralKeysOnUnshapedArrays, restrictReturnTypes, runTaintAnalysis.
  Tambem nao se acrescenta lista <forbiddenFunctions> (ex.: print_r): seria uma
  regra escrita pelo usuario, nao uma verificacao da ferramenta.

  Execucao (na raiz do projeto Laravel):
    vendor/bin/psalm -c psalm-completa.xml
  (acrescente a opcao no-cache, com dois hifens, para ignorar o cache)
-->
<psalm
    errorLevel="1"
    resolveFromConfigFile="true"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xmlns="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://getpsalm.org/schema/config vendor/vimeo/psalm/config.xsd"
    findUnusedCode="true"
    findUnusedVariablesAndParams="true"
    findUnusedPsalmSuppress="true"
    findUnusedBaselineEntry="true"
    findUnusedIssueHandlerSuppression="true"
    limitMethodComplexity="true"
>
    <projectFiles>
        <directory name="app" />
        <ignoreFiles>
            <directory name="vendor" />
        </ignoreFiles>
    </projectFiles>
</psalm>
